          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Badugi, a lowball draw game where the best hand has four different suits and low cards.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). In Badugi each card in the hand must be from a different suit; duplicate suits weaken the hand. Lowest card in each suit counts.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit; ace is low. The best Badugi hand is four low cards in four different suits (e.g. A-2-3-4 of different suits). Pairs and same-suit cards are not wanted.',
